#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"GwenRename is a batch renaming tool. It was created as an external tool for "
"<ulink url=\"http://dolphin.kde.org/\">&dolphin;</ulink> and <ulink url="
"\"http://www.konqueror.org/\">&konqueror;</ulink>. As that, the files/"
"folders to be renamed are passed to it as command line parameters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main goal is to have a batch renaming tool that's easy and light enough "
"for every day use. If you are looking for a more compound and featured "
"renaming tool, you should have a look at Dominik Seichter's <ulink url="
"\"http://www.krename.net\">KRename</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:70 index.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid "How does it work?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"GwenRename has an easy to use interface (take a look at the <link linkend="
"\"main-window\">main window</link>), where the user can adjust the renaming "
"parameters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"GwenRename accepts a number of command line parameters (the items to be "
"renamed), and creates a new filename for each file passed to it, using the "
"following scheme:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;prefix&gt;&lt;name&gt;&lt;number&gt;&lt;suffix&gt;.&lt;extension&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each of these fields is user configurable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Special attention has been given so that there is no chance to overwrite or "
"delete already existing files. All comparisons between existing filenames "
"and filenames to be used for renaming are case in-sensitive, so it can be "
"used even on a vfat filesystem."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using GwenRename"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "GwenRename has two modes of operation: file mode and folder mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid "file mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this mode only files can be selected for renaming"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "folder mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this mode only folders can be selected for renaming"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These two modes cannot be mixed (&ie; you cannot rename files and folders at "
"the same renaming session)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "Launching GwenRename"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "The program can be launched using any of the following ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gwenrename <option>[list of files]</option></userinput> (refer to "
"<link linkend=\"file-mode\">File mode</link>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gwenrename <option>[list of folders]</option></userinput> (refer "
"to <link linkend=\"folder-mode\">Folder mode</link>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gwenrename <option>[folder]</option></userinput> (refer to <link "
"linkend=\"mode-selection\">Mode selection</link>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gwenrename</userinput> (refer to <link linkend=\"input-folder-"
"selection\">Input folder selection</link>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on the way the program was launched, one of the following will "
"occur:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "File mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <link linkend=\"main-window\">main window</link> will be displayed, "
"making the selected files available for renaming."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "Folder mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <link linkend=\"main-window\">main window</link> will be displayed, "
"making the selected folders available for renaming."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mode selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Passing a single folder as a parameter, will make GwenRename display the "
"Mode Selection window, shown below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "The user can now either click on:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Rename folder</guibutton> to rename the selected folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>or</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Rename files</guibutton> to rename the files contained in it"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid "Input folder selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When no parameters are passed to the program, the folder selection dialog "
"will be displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The contents of the selected folder will be displayed in GwenRename list, so "
"that the user can select the files/folders to rename."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Launching from &konqueror; and &dolphin;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select desired files/folders, right click and select <guimenu>Actions</"
"guimenu> / <guimenu>Rename with GwenRename</guimenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "Launching from the Command Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "To rename all jpg files in folder /path/to/files, type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>gwenrename <option>/path/to/files/*.jpg</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid "To rename folders fold-1 and fold-4 in folder /path/to/files, type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gwenrename <option>/path/to/files/fold-1 /path/to/files/fold-4</"
"option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select either to rename my-files folder in /path/to/files or files/"
"folders under /path/to/files/my-files , type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>gwenrename <option>/path/to/files/my-files</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>GwenRename Main Window</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>GwenRename Main Window</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "GwenRename Main Window is divided in two parts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The ListView part</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It displays the items contained in the target folder, and provides the "
"ability to add or remove items to the <link linkend=\"items-management"
"\">Items List</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Renaming options adjustment part"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It provides all necessary options to adjust the format of the new filename "
"for each item in the <link linkend=\"items-management\">Items List</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The ListView part</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Items to be renamed (members of the <link linkend=\"items-management\">Items "
"List</link>) are denoted by the existence of the State Icon, an icon present "
"in the first column of the ListView, which displays the expected renaming "
"result, given the current <link linkend=\"options\">Renaming options</link>, "
"as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<inlineequation> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"hi16-"
"app-gwenrename.png\"/> </imageobject> </inlinemediaobject> </inlineequation> "
"The item is expected to be renamed successfully"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<inlineequation> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref="
"\"gray16-app-gwenrename.png\"/> </imageobject> </inlinemediaobject> </"
"inlineequation> The item will not be renamed, because the old and new "
"filename is the same"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<inlineequation> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref="
"\"button_cancel.png\"/> </imageobject> </inlinemediaobject> </"
"inlineequation> The item will not be renamed, because that would overwrite "
"an existing item. In fact, renaming is disabled until this condition is "
"resolved (by readjusting the <link linkend=\"options\">Renaming options</"
"link>). This icon may vary as it depends on the active icon theme."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing items in GwenRename"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid "GwenRename works with two different sets of items (files or folders)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Items List"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These are the items (files or folders) to be renamed. They are marked by a "
"state icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Items List can be formed by passing the items' names as command line "
"parameters to GwenRename, by double clicking an item in the ListView, or by "
"using the ListView context menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Selection List"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These are the selected items in the ListView. They can be added or removed "
"from the Items List, used to create a new Items List, etc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A selection can be formed as usual (click to select a single item, Shift-"
"Click to select items in a row, Ctrl-Click to add a single item to the "
"selection), or by using the ListView context menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "Context menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By right clicking on the Items List, the context menu is available to the "
"user. When <guimenu>Show all items</guimenu> is not checked, a reduced "
"version of the menu is displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "The functions available through the context menu are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "List management"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These menu entries modify the current <link linkend=\"items-management"
"\">Items List</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens the selected item in its default program"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open file with"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens the selected item in a user selected program"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add to list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adds the selected items (items in the Selection List) to the Items List"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove from list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Removes the selected items (items in the Selection List) from the Items List"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid "Invert list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Removes from the Items List all items that were contained within, and "
"inserts all items that were not."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the target folder contains files and sub-folders, a type inversion "
"accrues when all items of one type are selected. For example, when all "
"folders are already in the Items List, they will be removed after its "
"execution, and all files will be inserted to it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create list from selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Replaces the Items List with the selected items (items in the Selection List)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selection management"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These menu entries modify the current <link linkend=\"items-management"
"\">Selection List</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "All items"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selects all items"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "All items of selected type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selects all items of selected type, that is all files or all folders"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "Invert current selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects all items that were not selected previously, and deselects all items "
"that were"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create selection from list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selects all items contained in the Items List"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Items containing a string"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selects items based on a search string. It uses the <ulink url=\"search-"
"window.html\">Items Selection Window</ulink>"
msgstr ""

